---Create a key
---
---Create a key in a given region specified by the `region` parameter. You can use keys to encrypt or decrypt arbitrary payloads, to sign and verify messages or to generate data encryption keys. **Data encryption keys are not stored in Key Manager**.
---
---`POST /key-manager/v1alpha1/regions/{region}/keys`
---@param input? scaleway.key_manager_v1alpha1.CreateKeyRequest
---@return scaleway.key_manager_v1alpha1.Key? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_key(input) end

---Decrypt an encrypted payload
---
---Decrypt an encrypted payload using an existing key, specified by the `key_id` parameter. The maximum payload size that can be decrypted is equivalent to the encrypted output of 64 KB of data (around 131 KB).
---
---`POST /key-manager/v1alpha1/regions/{region}/keys/{key_id}/decrypt`
---@param input scaleway.key_manager_v1alpha1.DecryptRequest
---@return scaleway.key_manager_v1alpha1.DecryptResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:decrypt(input) end

---Delete a key
---
---Permanently delete a key specified by the `region` and `key_id` parameters. This action is irreversible. Any data encrypted with this key, including data encryption keys, will no longer be decipherable.
---
---`DELETE /key-manager/v1alpha1/regions/{region}/keys/{key_id}`
---@param input scaleway.key_manager_v1alpha1.DeleteKeyRequest
---@return scaleway.key_manager_v1alpha1.DeleteKeyResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_key(input) end

---Delete key material
---
---Delete previously imported key material. This renders the associated cryptographic key unusable for any operation. The key's origin must be `external`.
---
---`POST /key-manager/v1alpha1/regions/{region}/keys/{key_id}/delete-key-material`
---@param input scaleway.key_manager_v1alpha1.DeleteKeyMaterialRequest
---@return scaleway.key_manager_v1alpha1.DeleteKeyMaterialResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_key_material(input) end

---Disable key
---
---Disable a given key, preventing it to be used for cryptographic operations. Disabling a key renders it unusable. You must specify the `region` and `key_id` parameters.
---
---`POST /key-manager/v1alpha1/regions/{region}/keys/{key_id}/disable`
---@param input scaleway.key_manager_v1alpha1.DisableKeyRequest
---@return scaleway.key_manager_v1alpha1.Key? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:disable_key(input) end

---Enable key
---
---Enable a given key to be used for cryptographic operations. Enabling a key allows you to make a disabled key usable again. You must specify the `region` and `key_id` parameters.
---
---`POST /key-manager/v1alpha1/regions/{region}/keys/{key_id}/enable`
---@param input scaleway.key_manager_v1alpha1.EnableKeyRequest
---@return scaleway.key_manager_v1alpha1.Key? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:enable_key(input) end

---Encrypt a payload
---
---Encrypt a payload using an existing key, specified by the `key_id` parameter. The maximum payload size that can be encrypted is 64 KB of plaintext.
---
---`POST /key-manager/v1alpha1/regions/{region}/keys/{key_id}/encrypt`
---@param input scaleway.key_manager_v1alpha1.EncryptRequest
---@return scaleway.key_manager_v1alpha1.EncryptResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:encrypt(input) end

